Rule 1 (input tensors must have broadcastable shapes.)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ∀i ∈ [0, (if ndim(v_1) > ndim(v_2) then ndim(v_1) - 1 else ndim(v_2) - 1)] : (i ≥ ndim(v_1) ∨ i ≥ ndim(v_2) ∨ (shape(v_1, (ndim(v_1) - 1) - i) = shape(v_2, (ndim(v_2) - 1) - i)) ∨ (shape(v_1, (ndim(v_1) - 1) - i) = 1) ∨ (shape(v_2, (ndim(v_2) - 1) - i) = 1))
>>
Rule 2 (if other is a tensor, it should have the same dtype as input if input is not bool.)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= if dtype_(v_1) ≠ 0 then dtype_(v_1) = dtype_(v_2)
>>
Rule 3 (if other is a float, it should be within the min and max range of the input tensor.)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : float} |= min(v_1) ≤ v_2 ∧ v_2 ≤ max(v_1)
>>
Rule 4 (if other is a tensor, the size of the tensor must match the size of the input tensor at non-singleton dimension)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ∀i ∈ [0, (if ndim(v_1) > ndim(v_2) then ndim(v_1) - 1 else ndim(v_2) - 1)] : (i ≥ ndim(v_1) ∨ i ≥ ndim(v_2) ∨ shape(v_1, (ndim(v_1) - 1) - i) = shape(v_2, (ndim(v_2) - 1) - i) ∨ (shape(v_1, (ndim(v_1) - 1) - i) = 1) ∨ (shape(v_2, (ndim(v_2) - 1) - i) = 1))
>>
Rule 5 (if other is a tensor, its shape should be equal to the shape of input tensor.)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2) ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i)
